Below is a ready‑to‑paste snippet that you can drop into any HTML page.  
It embeds the map centered on the library, shows a custom marker for the **State Library**, and draws three circles at the coordinates you supplied.

```html
<!-- 1️⃣  Embed the map (static image) -->
<img
  src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/staticmap?center=34.052235,-118.243683&zoom=15&size=600x400&maptype=roadmap&markers=color:blue%7C34.052235,-118.243683&key=YOUR_API_KEY"
  alt="State Library map"
  width="600"
  height="400"
/>

<!-- 2️⃣  (Optional)  If you prefer an interactive map, use the Google Maps JavaScript API -->
<div id="map" style="width:600px;height:400px;"></div>
<script>
  function initMap() {
    const center = { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 };
    const map = new google.maps.Map(document.getElementById('map'), {
      zoom: 15,
      center: center,
      mapTypeId: 'roadmap'
    });

    // Marker for the State Library
    new google.maps.Marker({
      position: center,
      map: map,
      title: 'State Library'
    });

    // Three circles
    const circleCoords = [
      { lat: 34.052235, lng: -118.243683 },
      { lat: 34.053690, lng: -118.2423732 },
      { lat: 34.05381,  lng: -118.242751 }
    ];

    circleCoords.forEach(coord => {
      new google.maps.Circle({
        strokeColor: '#FF0000',
        strokeOpacity: 0.8,
        strokeWeight: 2,
        fillColor: '#FF0000',
        fillOpacity: 0.35,
        map: map,
        center: coord,
        radius: 50   // radius in meters – adjust as needed
      });
    });
  }
</script>
<script async defer
  src="https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/js?key=YOUR_API_KEY&callback=initMap">
</script>
```

### What the code does

| Step | What happens | Notes |
|------|--------------|-------|
| 1️⃣ | The `<img>` tag pulls a **static map** from Google Maps. The `markers` parameter places a blue pin at the library’s coordinates. | Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key. |
| 2️⃣ | The `<div id="map">` block creates an **interactive map** using the JavaScript API. | Only one of the two blocks (static or interactive) is needed. |
| 2️⃣a | `initMap()` centers the map on the library and adds a marker titled “State Library.” | |
| 2️⃣b | Three `google.maps.Circle` objects are drawn at the coordinates you listed. | Radius is set to 50 m; change it if you need a different size. |

Feel free to tweak the marker colors, circle styles, or map size to match your site’s design. If you run into any issues (e.g., API key restrictions, billing), let me know!

