Below is a quick‑start guide for adding a **SoundCloud playback widget** to any web page (HTML, React, Vue, etc.).  
I’ll cover the three most common ways:

| Method | When to use | What you need |
|--------|-------------|---------------|
| **oEmbed / iframe** | Simple “just‑play” embed, no JS needed | Track URL or ID |
| **Widget API** | Want to control playback (play/pause, volume, events) | Track URL or ID + a bit of JS |
| **REST API + custom player** | Full control, custom UI, analytics, etc. | API key, OAuth token, track ID |

---

## 1️⃣ oEmbed / iframe (Easiest)

```html
<!-- Replace YOUR_TRACK_URL with the SoundCloud track link -->
<iframe width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
  src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=YOUR_TRACK_URL&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false">
</iframe>
```

* **Pros** – No JavaScript, works in any browser.  
* **Cons** – Limited interactivity (you can’t programmatically pause or seek).

---

## 2️⃣ Widget API (JavaScript control)

1. **Add the Widget script** (once per page):

```html
<script src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/api.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
```

2. **Create the iframe** (same as above, but give it an `id`):

```html
<iframe id="sc-player" width="100%" height="166" scrolling="no" frameborder="no"
  src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=YOUR_TRACK_URL&color=%23ff5500&auto_play=false&hide_related=false&show_comments=true&show_user=true&show_reposts=false">
</iframe>
```

3. **Control it with JavaScript**:

```js
// Wait for the widget script to load
window.onload = function () {
  const widgetIframe = document.getElementById('sc-player');
  const widget = SC.Widget(widgetIframe);

  // Play the track
  widget.play();

  // Pause
  widget.pause();

  // Seek to 30 seconds
  widget.seekTo(30000);

  // Listen for events
  widget.bind(SC.Widget.Events.FINISH, function () {
    console.log('Track finished!');
  });

  // Get track info
  widget.getCurrentSound(function (sound) {
    console.log('Now playing:', sound.title, 'by', sound.user.username);
  });
};
```

> **Tip** – If you’re using a framework (React/Vue/Angular), wrap the iframe in a component and use the `useEffect`/`mounted` hook to initialize the widget.

---

## 3️⃣ REST API + Custom Player (Full control)

If you want a completely custom UI (e.g., a custom progress bar, volume slider, or analytics), you’ll need to:

1. **Get an API key** – Register an app at <https://soundcloud.com/you/apps> to receive a `client_id`.  
2. **Fetch track data** (you can use the built‑in `getTrackInfo` function if you have a track ID):

```js
// Example using the provided function
const trackInfo = await functions.getTrackInfo({ track_id: '123456789' });
console.log(trackInfo.title, trackInfo.artist);
```

3. **Use the track’s `stream_url`** (append `?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID`) to stream audio:

```js
const audio = new Audio(`https://api.soundcloud.com/tracks/123456789/stream?client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID`);
audio.play();
```

4. **Build your UI** – Use standard HTML5 `<audio>` controls or a custom UI with JavaScript.

> **Note** – The free tier of the SoundCloud API has rate limits. For production use, consider caching track data and handling OAuth if you need user‑specific data.

---

## Quick Checklist

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| 1 | Decide on the level of interactivity you need. |
| 2 | Get the track URL or ID. |
| 3 | Add the iframe (oEmbed) or the widget script (Widget API). |
| 4 | (Optional) Add custom JS to control playback. |
| 5 | Test on desktop and mobile browsers. |
| 6 | If you need analytics or custom UI, use the REST API + `<audio>` element. |

---

### Need a specific track ID?

If you already know the track ID (e.g., `123456789`), let me know and I can generate a ready‑to‑paste snippet for you.  
If you only have the track URL, just replace `YOUR_TRACK_URL` in the examples above with the full URL (e.g., `https://soundcloud.com/artist/track-name`).

Happy embedding! 🎶

